# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv
venv/
.env
# …and every suffixed variant. `.env` alone is an EXACT match, so the
# `.env.bak.20260819` rollback copy sitting in service/ — live GROK/DEEPSEEK/
# DEEPINFRA keys and ADMIN_PASSWORD — was one `git add -A` from a commit, and
# this repo feeds a public mirror. The example file stays tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS
.DS_Store

# Node
# No trailing slash: a directory-only pattern does not match a SYMLINK, and both
# worktree node_modules here are symlinks into the main checkout — so they kept
# showing up as untracked.
node_modules
.next/
dist/

# Local state — anything containing real session data, account data, or secrets
service/proxies.json
service/secrets.json
service/secrets/
service/chatterly.db
service/chatterly.db-journal
service/chatterly.db-wal
service/chatterly.db-shm
service/chatterly.db.bak*
service/chatterly.db.devbak*
*.devbak.*
service/sessions/
service/storyboard_cache/
service/vault_thumbs/
service/vault_posters/
service/s4s_media/
service/vault_images/
service/img_cache/
.run_public/

# Secrets / one-off captures
# Google OAuth client + cached token of the retired push_to_sheets automation.
# credentials.json holds a client_secret; token.json a live refresh/access
# token — old checkouts may still have them; never commit either.
credentials.json
token.json
service/credentials.json
service/token.json
claudflaretoken
my_Curl_session.example
of_calls_tail.txt
errors
bookmark_error_curl
__pycache__/

# Large local DB / session snapshots — never commit (100s of MB, contain live data)
*.bak
service/*.pre_*
service/sessions.*.tar.gz
chatterly.db.pre_*

# HAR network captures — large + contain live session cookies/tokens/PII
*.har

# Legacy reference dump (336MB, includes credentials.json) — local-only
OF_AUTOMATIONV1/

# Local Claude Code config (machine-specific settings + skills)
.claude/

# graphify output — regenerable, and it distills private design docs + carries
# absolute laptop paths, so it must never be committed (it reached the PUBLIC
# mirror once). Any level: root graphify-out/, service/graphify-out/, archives.
graphify-out/
graphify-deep/

# Settings export/import backups (local dev preimages — contain account settings; never commit)
service/data/settings_backups/
# Forge runtime DBs (state, not code; .omc/plans/*.md ARE committed)
.omc/forge.db
.omc/forge.db-*

# Local sim/scratch harnesses + prod-data replays (never commit — throwaway)
service/chatterly.sandbox.db
# …and its WAL sidecars, like chatterly.db above. Without these a test run leaves
# two untracked files in `git status`, which is how a throwaway gets swept into a
# commit by an `add -A`.
service/chatterly.sandbox.db-wal
service/chatterly.sandbox.db-shm
service/_sim_*.py
service/_live_*.py
service/_probe_*.py
service/_verify_*.py
service/_apply_*.py
service/_proto_*.py
CONVO_RUNS.md

# Real OF conversation transcripts (creator + fan message bodies). Local only.
CONVO_RUN*.md

# ── Never commit: real people's data ────────────────────────────────
#
# Everything here was written by a tool or a debugging session that had live
# data in front of it. Each pattern is a class that actually reached a commit
# or a public sync at least once, not a hypothetical.

# Conversation dumps — verbatim OF message bodies, prices, purchase outcomes
# and one fan's spending history. `CONVO_RUNSold.md` slipped an ALL-CAPS
# filename filter because of its lowercase tail, so match loosely.
[Cc][Oo][Nn][Vv][Oo]*.md
*_CONVO*.md
*CHAT*.md
!plans/*.md
# spec-auto design artefacts (specs, tickets) are not chat logs — re-include them
!docs/spec/*.md
!docs/spec/*/*.md
!.scratch/*/issues/*.md
# …and nested plan docs. One level of whitelist left plans/hook-upsell/
# untracked while seven sibling plan dirs were tracked, so ten comments in
# ai_chatter.py cited a path no checkout contained.
!plans/**/*.md

# Probe/report pages. These embed the creator's own media as base64 data URIs —
# a single file is hundreds of her photographs, inline, in git forever.
vault-reports/
*_audit_*.html
*_review_*.html
*_recheck_*.html
flags_*.html
filter_gaps_*.html

# Anything a probe writes next to itself.
service/*.html
service/_out_/

# Cat-sticker prototype — 28M of gifs + regenerable build artifacts
# (build_*.py, candidates/, __pycache__). Stays UNTRACKED by ruling; the
# gifs are a bulk asset set, not source.
cat_stickers/

# Convo reader output — one big self-contained HTML. Regenerable.
convo_review.html

# Per-machine container limit overrides (and any other local compose tweak).
# Compose merges this automatically. It is per-machine by definition, so it
# must never be committed.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Priority-lane counters. `server.py` flushes these at MODULE SCOPE, so merely
# importing server writes the file — and service/.env points DATABASE_URL at the
# repo, so an ad-hoc `python -c "import server"` from service/ (or anything
# reaching vault_frames' lazy `import server`) drops it here rather than in the
# docker volume where prod keeps it. Its `accounts` keys are live OF account ids,
# so an `add -A` sweep is one command from publishing them.
service/priority_lane_stats.json
priority_lane_stats.json

# Phase backups taken during the Fansly go-live (live account data, ~1.2G each)
service/chatterly.pre-*.db
service/chatterly.pre-*.db-shm
service/chatterly.pre-*.db-wal

# Review-loop working artifacts. Every review pass drops findings docs, scope
# notes and .patch snapshots here; 66 of them were one `add -A` from the tree on
# 2026-09-06. The four files already tracked stay tracked — an ignore rule does
# not untrack. Add a `!scratchpad/<name>` line for anything worth keeping.
scratchpad/

# Probe breadcrumbs: carry a real account id in the filename and live OF
# object ids inside. Written by scripts/probe_vault_upload.py on the host only.
service/.probe_vault_carriers_*.json

# Vault batch-upload spool: creator media in transit to OnlyFans, plus run
# state carrying real account ids and OF post ids. Host-only, never committed.
service/vault_spool/

# SQLite DBs and session/chatter secrets — never tracked. Test DBs are built
# at runtime.
*.db
.chatter_secret
.session_secret
service/.chatter_secret
service/.session_secret
chatterly.db
app/chatterly.db

# Landing site (web/): build output and deps
web/dist
web/node_modules

# local mirror of infloww.com, never commit
infloww.com/

# parody blog posts may contain "chat" in the slug; the *CHAT*.md rule above is case-insensitive on macOS
!web/src/blog/*.md
